## Who can use CRM

CRM is a suite. It is available once your firm has enabled the sales AI employee. Tenant admins can always use it; anyone else needs access granted to their department or to them personally.

**Where:** **Admin** › **Suites** › **CRM** (the **CRM settings** page). Tenant admins only.

| Card | Use |
|---|---|
| **Access** | The departments and people who can use CRM. Access given to a department follows its members. If nobody is chosen, only tenant admins can use CRM. |
| **Team leads** | The people who can edit the stages and vocabularies, edit the follow-up settings and set personal targets. Only named people can be team leads, not departments. Being a team lead does not let someone see more opportunities. |
| **View all opportunities** | The people who can see every opportunity in the firm. Only named people can be added. They can read every opportunity, but change only those in their own reporting line. |
| **Currency** | The **CRM currency** used for new opportunities and targets. Changing it does not convert the amounts already recorded. |
| **Contracts**, **Issuing entities**, **Contract signatories**, **Contract layouts** | Contract settings. See [1 · Contract settings](/en/crm/templates/). |

## Who sees which opportunities

| Person | Sees | Can change |
|---|---|---|
| **Tenant admin** | Every opportunity. | Every opportunity. |
| On the **View all opportunities** list | Every opportunity. | Only those in their reporting line. |
| Anyone else with CRM | The opportunities of their reporting line: those where the person in charge (PIC), the Manager in charge, the Director in charge or the creator is themselves or someone who reports to them. | The same opportunities. |

An opportunity you can see but not change is marked **View only**: you can read it and post notes, but not change its fields, stage, owner, services or contracts. A board column may say **There may be opportunities here you can't see**.

## Where CRM is

Select **Workspace** in the side bar and choose the **CRM** workspace. Its side bar has:

| Group | Entry | See |
|---|---|---|
| **Sales** | **Opportunity** — the board of all opportunities. The number on it is the count of contracts waiting for your approval. | [The opportunity board](/en/crm/opportunities/) |
| **Dashboard** | **Dashboard** — sales reports and targets. | [Dashboard and targets](/en/crm/dashboard/) |
| **Catalog** | **Services & Packages** — what your firm sells. | [2 · Services & Packages](/en/crm/services-packages/) |
